# Agent consistency (governance artifacts)

When you **edit** paths matched by this rule's `globs`, keep workflow artifacts aligned in the **same turn**. Pair with [agent-agents-md-maintenance.mdc](agent-agents-md-maintenance.mdc) for agent/kanban **skills**; this rule covers **rules**, **reference tables**, and **AGENTS.md** parity. End-of-turn prompts: [agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md) §6g. **Artifact parity table:** [agent-triage/reference.md](../skills/agent-triage/reference.md) § Consistency matrix.

## Before handoff — four check types

### 1. Schema consistency

- [ ] Reference § Failure patterns tables use five columns (Signature, Trigger snippet, Fix pattern, Skill, Rule) — [agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md) §6f
- [ ] Rules cite **Signature** only — **no Fix pattern prose** copied from reference rows

### 2. Routing consistency

- [ ] [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) **Every turn** steps match [agent-triage/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-triage/SKILL.md) (incl. §1b when present)
- [ ] [agent-routing.mdc](agent-routing.mdc) turn lifecycle matches AGENTS.md
- [ ] No artifact still references deprecated steps (grep stale lifecycle labels in governance docs)

### 3. Card-type consistency

- [ ] Every kanban label in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) card types table has a matching `kanban-*.mdc` and section in [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) — includes **`plan`** → [kanban-plan-cards.mdc](kanban-plan-cards.mdc), **`feedback`** → [kanban-feedback-cards.mdc](kanban-feedback-cards.mdc) (Signature: `feedback-label-kanban`, `kanban-cursor-mode-gates`)
- [ ] New label type → update all three in the same turn

### 4. Failure-pattern consistency

- [ ] New **Signature** → row in owning `reference.md` (cross-cutting: [agent-self-evaluation/reference.md](../skills/agent-self-evaluation/reference.md); hooks: [pre-commit-workflow/reference.md](../skills/pre-commit-workflow/reference.md))
- [ ] New **Signature** → [agent-triage/reference.md](../skills/agent-triage/reference.md) § Failure pattern routing (or §1b examples)
- [ ] Rules that mention a pattern cite **Signature** — grep signature exists in a reference table

