## Do not

- Duplicate Fix pattern prose from reference tables into `.mdc` files
- Add a Signature to a rule without a reference row
- Change triage lifecycle without updating AGENTS.md and agent-routing.mdc

**Periodic audit:** [kanban-markdown/SKILL.md](../skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md) § Periodic AGENTS.md governance audit — `python3 scripts/create_governance_audit_card.py`.

**Drift alert format:** when reporting parity mismatches, use prefixes from [agent-triage/reference.md](../skills/agent-triage/reference.md) § Drift alert examples — cite matrix row or audit checklist item; Signature only in rules.

## When to emit drift alerts

| Trigger | Emit where |
| ------- | ---------- |
| This turn **edited** a path matching this rule's `globs` | Run matrix + four check types before handoff ([agent-triage/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-triage/SKILL.md) § Governance drift detection) |
| Parity fails and is **not** fixed same turn | **Context load** note, [agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md](../skills/agent-self-evaluation/SKILL.md) §6g, handoff `- **Drift alerts:**` (one prefixed line per mismatch) |
| User runs / pastes `check_governance_parity.py` output | Context load + §6g + handoff `- **Drift alerts:**`; script spawns **todo** fix cards (epic `GovernanceDriftFix`; consolidated by root cause — **`GovernanceDriftAlert` closed**) unless `--no-spawn-cards` |
| User approved **temporary** drift | `KNOWN_DRIFT: <artifact pair> — <reason>[; expires: <date or note>]` in handoff — see reference § KNOWN_DRIFT |

**Do not** emit drift alerts on every turn — only when governance globs were edited or user runs/pastes `check_governance_parity.py` output. Read-only turns → N/A.
